  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004888/assets/de15e1e9433a3560cbc8268904f4f62fbbb721c3b5b9a700c59fea0941829406.png)\n\nThe area of the shaded region between the curve $y={x}^{3}+8$ and the $x$-axis is given by the integral expression below. What is the value of $a?$\n\n$$\nA={\\int }_{a}^{2}({x}^{3}+8)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "To get $a$, we need to find the $x$-intercepts of the curve $y={x}^{3}+8.$ \n\nWe solve the equation for $y=0$: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3}+8 & =y \\\\ {x}^{3}+8 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{3} & =-8 \\\\ x & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=-2.$",
